=== layout: two-panels

# Nucleotides join to forma DNA or an RNA chain

@left

![A-G-C polynucleotide schematic](assets/lect02d-dna_structure_overview/agc_schematic.drawn.svg)

@right

- Polynucleotide chains have a 5&prime;-phosphate at one end and a 3&prime;-OH on the other end.
- The 5&prime; end terminates with a phosphate group.
- Phosphate is linked to the 5&prime; carbon and to the 3&prime; carbon by phosphodiester bonds.
- The 3&prime; end terminates with hydroxyl (-OH).

